WEBVTT

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:03.350
All right. Let's start
with first base pickoffs.

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:08.530
Chisato, pretend you're on the
opposing team and try stealing a base.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:09.820
Roger.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:15.050
Mutsuko and Anita, do everything
you can to stop Chisato from stealing.

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:16.660
We're starting with runners?

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.870
Yeah, we won't have time otherwise.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.100
All right. Play!

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.340
Balk!

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:25.880
Huh?

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:30.840
No good. You can't stop halfway on
a pickoff attempt if your foot's on the rubber.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:36.590
Balk!

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:37.930
Again?!

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.730
You need to speed it up.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.320
All right. Again.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.890
<i>What a nag.</i>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.850
<i>I'm trying my best here...</i>

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:48.440
Balk!

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.270
Huh?

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.030
Heya.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.580
Your glove didn't come to a stop.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.120
In the set position, a balk's called if your
glove doesn't come to a complete stop.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:04.830
Heya.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.420
All right. Again!

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.130
Again?!

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:11.950
Senpai, she ain't gettin'
it perfect by tomorrow.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:15.130
All this'll do is make us
self-destruct 'cause we're focusin'

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:17.530
on the runner an' forgettin' 'bout the batter!

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:21.100
Yeah. As a pitcher, I agree with what she said.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.810
It's impossible to learn quick pickoffs
 and slide steps in one day.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.740
Someone who's never pitched
before wouldn't understand.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.900
I never said this was going to be easy.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:39.120
But as we're up against a running team,
I want to take the fight to them!

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:44.500
If we can't shackle Seiwa's runners,
we will lose tomorrow.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.460
We still have time.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.040
You can never be fully prepared,

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:52.880
but if there's still stuff we can do,
I want to do it before we take them on!

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.770
It's all good. Let's get on with it already, Daigo.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.940
<b>Yanagigawa</b>

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.940
<b>Atsumori</b>

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:42.780
<b>Extreme Small Ball</b>

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:44.070
Sorry I'm late, everyone!

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.280
Hey, ace! What time d'ya call this?

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:50.370
I'm so sorry.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.460
I got stuck in traffic.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:55.510
Wait, Shigeno isn't with you?

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:58.840
Huh? Uh, no, Daigo isn't with me...

00:03:58.840 --> 00:03:59.920
What?!

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.340
Oh, boy. Maybe Daigo's goofed this one.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.620
Yikes. Does this mean we have to forfeit?

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.390
<i>Do I smell the sweet scent of a forfeit?</i>

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.710
<i>Day off, here I come!</i>

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:14.670
Sensei, could you call
Daigo's house for us, please?

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.230
Oh, uh, right.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.470
What the heck's he playin' at?

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:20.500
An' he's always actin' so high 'n' mighty...

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:21.760
Hey!

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.850
Daigo?!

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.370
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.370
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.370
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:30.370
Sorry, my bad.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.830
I got here early, so I ended up
watching the game before ours.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.500
Jeez. Don't scare us like that, Daigo.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.630
<i>The game before ours?</i>

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.830
<i>The winner of that game is who
we're playin' next if we win today.</i>

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:46.970
<i>He ain't figured out our pitchin' options yet,
but he's aimin' to win this all the same.</i>

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.850
Uh-oh. That's some fastball he's got.

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:01.420
I didn't know Seiwa had a power pitcher.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:04.070
If he's got breakin' balls too,
we're in deep trouble.

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:07.620
Urabe-kun's improved a whole lot.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.240
We can't afford to let them score.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.200
Well, we hardly know
anything about his game,

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.540
so we should be patient at the plate
and make him throw a lot in the early going.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.940
This may end up as a low-scoring game,

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:23.260
so every run scored and
every run saved is crucial!

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.780
Right!

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:26.220
Line up!

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:29.630
Bow!

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.890
Let's have a good game!

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.600
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.600
<b>Moriguchi</b>

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.600
<b>Miyata</b>

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.600
<b>Urabe</b>

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:36.400
<i>Batting first, second base, Moriguchi-kun.</i>

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.850
Play ball!

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.610
Go, Moriguchi!

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:50.160
<i>The speed of this team's
a real pain in the butt.</i>

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:53.490
<i>We hafta stop their leadoff from gettin' on base.</i>

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:55.680
<i>Please, Sakura-senpai.</i>

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:58.210
<i>Don't let this game be as far as we get.</i>

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:04.100
Ball!

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:07.550
Strike!

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:09.980
Strike!

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:13.380
<i>We got 'im cornered.</i>

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:17.730
<i>Or more likely, he's tryna get a read
on us and ain't interested in swingin'.</i>

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:21.360
<i>But it takes a lotta nerve and game sense</i>

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.440
<i>to wait till yer back's to
the wall before ya swing.</i>

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:28.900
<i>It ain't somethin' ya can do unless
ya got a good eye and a good swing.</i>

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.140
<i>Let's try to paint the black.</i>

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:37.550
Foul!

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:39.950
Ball!

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:42.670
<i>I figured this game'd be a chore...</i>

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:42.670
Ball!

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.910
Nice one, Moriguchi!

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:49.220
<i>...but it looks like we're gonna be here a while.</i>

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:52.890
Ball!

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.850
Ball four!

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:00.770
<i>Aw, man.</i>

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:03.980
<i>I was supposed to stop him
from getting on base.</i>

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:07.940
<i>Batting second, center field, Miyata-kun.</i>

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.370
<i>They're at it already, Senpai!</i>

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.400
<i>Let's counter 'em with our own speed!</i>

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:24.000
Huh? What do you mean, "don't do pickoffs"?

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.190
Whaddaya talkin' 'bout?!

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:29.670
Ya made us stay an' practice till this late an'
<i>now</i> yer tellin' us: "Yeah, don't bother, 'kay?"

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.810
Pfeh! Is this a joke?

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:35.440
So you're saying my pickoffs
aren't good enough, is that it?

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:37.140
No, that's not what I'm saying.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:41.460
Even though we were limited on time,
your pickoffs are pretty fast now.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.450
So what's the problem?!

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:46.940
The more pickoff attempts you make,
the easier it is for the opponent to run.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:49.670
Going for pickoffs all the time
 will get us nowhere.

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:52.320
Could you please start making sense, Daigo?

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:53.910
When stealing a base,

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:59.280
you need to size up the pitcher and
judge how much you can get away with.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:04.460
What I mean is, they have no idea how
quick your pickoffs are, or your technique.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:07.480
Since they're an experienced small ball team,

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:12.060
they shouldn't try anything
before they've figured all that out.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:13.390
<i>What?!</i>

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:15.510
<i>He's already goin' for it!</i>

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:16.850
Ball!

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:23.390
<i>Was it a feint?</i>

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:29.120
Basically, the more pickoffs you do,
the more the runners get a read on your game.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:32.610
At the start of the game, you want
to give away as little as possible.

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:36.500
<i>Sakura didn't attempt the pickoff.</i>

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:39.850
<i>But she must know we're a running team.</i>

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:44.790
<i>That woman on their bench
couldn't look less like a coach.</i>

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:48.750
<i>So is it Fuurin's catcher
who's calling the shots?</i>

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:53.720
<i>Or is it Shigeno,
who's listed as their captain?</i>

00:08:57.810 --> 00:08:59.350
Strike!

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.840
She's not going for the pickoff.

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:04.710
Even Moriguchi can't steal like that.

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.680
Then we'll make her throw one.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:19.700
Huh?

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:23.540
Seriously?!

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.190
That's a crazy long lead!

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.960
Wow. They're really messing with us.

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:32.950
<i>He told me not to attempt any pickoffs...</i>

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:37.090
<i>But if we get an out from it...
it'd be silly not to, right?!</i>

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:38.780
Safe!

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:40.800
He ain't out?

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.490
<i>Now you've seen our "super lead."</i>

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:45.370
<i>At first glance, it's a guaranteed out,</i>

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:49.810
<i>but when your focus is getting back on base,
even a lead longer than five meters is doable.</i>

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:54.480
<i>It's no good for stealing, because the runner
bolts back at the first sign of movement,</i>

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:57.310
<i>but it puts pressure on the battery,</i>

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:00.870
<i>and it's a great way to rattle your opponent.</i>

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:04.470
Just ignore him, Mutsuko!
Focus on the batter!

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.710
Yeah! Just let them hit!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:11.500
<i>If only it was that simple.
That's easy for the fielders to say.</i>

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:16.970
Ball!

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:19.430
Ball!

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:21.630
Ball!

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:23.500
Ball four!

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:28.040
<i>Unless the pitcher's really thick-skinned,
that just won't fly.</i>

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:32.770
No outs! Runners on first and second!

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:36.740
<i>Batting third, pitcher, Urabe-kun.</i>

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:38.650
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.200
<i>We're already in a tight spot.</i>

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.740
Okay! Let's go, let's go!

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.130
<i>No outs. Runners on first an' second.</i>

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:50.640
<i>What's this small ball team gonna try next?</i>

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:51.520
Play!

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:54.750
<i>At this rate, we're gonna get rolled.
I hafta do somethin'!</i>

00:10:55.870 --> 00:11:00.380
That said, I don't think we can
afford to forget pickoffs entirely.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:04.690
The important thing is to pick your moment.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:06.720
Pick your moment?

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:11.700
Yes. For example, the second baseman
stands a little way from their base,

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:14.310
so it entices the runner on second
to take a bigger lead, right?

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:18.150
But the distance from the catcher
to third base is quite short,

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:20.690
so stealing third's harder
than stealing second,

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:24.320
which means, if we can force them to take
shorter leads, baserunning won't be so easy.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:28.590
To put your opponent on guard
so they shorten their leads,

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:32.460
you need to show them you're
prepared to attempt a pickoff.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:35.750
Safe!

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:38.150
<i>That's good.</i>

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:41.240
<i>This team won't give up easily.</i>

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:44.140
<i>If we play this right, there's a chance
we can get a double play here.</i>

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:47.110
<i>This team's pretty good.</i>

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:49.850
<i>They've come up with a strategy
to counter our small ball.</i>

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:54.130
Ball!

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:59.110
<i>But the more caution you exercise,
the more you play into our hands.</i>

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:03.170
<i>We've been meticulously cultivating
this style of play for two years now,</i>

00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:05.590
<i>with the third-years at its heart.</i>

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.200
<i>It's not just about the speed,</i>

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:11.980
<i>but the heightened skill and awareness
that comes with aiming for the next base.</i>

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:17.290
<i>With this baserunning revolution,
our players have started seeing returns.</i>

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:19.940
Ball!

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:23.760
<i>And now they've realized...</i>

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:27.680
<i>Being fast on your feet
cuts your opponents deep.</i>

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.640
Come on now...

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:31.560
Mutsuko...

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:38.870
<i>They're still middle schoolers. They find it
a struggle just to hit and pitch straight.</i>

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:40.730
<i>With runners drawing their attention,</i>

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.550
<i>it's only natural for the
pitcher to lose their rhythm.</i>

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:46.950
<i>We haven't stolen a single base yet,</i>

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:50.410
<i>but they've scared
themselves into this position.</i>

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:53.970
<i>Don't fall to pieces, Senpai!</i>

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:57.380
<i>Ya gotta know ya can't just
worry 'bout 'em stealin'!</i>

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:00.530
Ball!

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:04.610
Ball!

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:06.130
Ball four!

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.980
All right!

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:09.100
No outs, bases loaded!

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:12.310
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Suzuki-kun.</i>

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.730
<i>Ya see now? This is what I was sayin' yesterday.</i>

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:21.210
<i>Like I told ya, get Sakura-senpai worryin'
'bout the runners an' she'll self-destruct.</i>

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:23.940
Anita!

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:26.800
Let's step out and take a—

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:28.070
Play!

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:28.610
Time—

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:30.280
Oh boy.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:38.670
<i>I need to throw a strike...</i>

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:40.260
<i>A strike!</i>

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.340
<i>We ain't got no choice.</i>

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:44.340
<i>I'm callin' a timeout after this pitch.</i>

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:47.010
<i>I have to throw... a strike!</i>

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:54.930
Right field!

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:00.060
<i>They got us.</i>

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:03.440
That's our first run.

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:04.730
Right on time.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:06.650
Go!

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:13.490
What?!

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:14.580
For real?!

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:22.670
Safe!

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:23.880
Second!

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:25.590
I don't think so!

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:27.690
All right! He's cornered!

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:31.340
Back home!

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:37.930
Safe!

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.330
Strike! You're out!

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:00.520
Out!

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:02.410
Three outs!

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:03.580
Change sides!

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:04.500
We did it!

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:07.710
A strikeout double-play?

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:10.350
I wanted to bag us another run.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:11.790
That was close.

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:14.230
That catcher's got a decent arm.

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:19.060
I told you to run so we could see her arm,
and burn our baserunning into their minds.

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:21.850
Two runs without 
a base hit is very good.

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:24.080
Now, focus on your pitching.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.110
Yes, sir.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:28.520
Dang. They're way too cocky.

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:30.360
Nice job, Anita.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:33.320
Well, at least they're gonna
think twice 'bout stealin' now.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:37.080
Sakura-senpai, ya can stop
gettin' yerself so worked up.

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:41.280
I'll cut 'em all down to size,
so stop worryin' an' just pitch.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:45.550
We can't help ya if ya start
workin' yerself up into a panic.

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:47.500
Hey, Anita!

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:50.630
What the hell was that play earlier?!

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:51.220
Huh?

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.540
Don't just "huh?" me!

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:55.930
I'm talking about that
close play on their first run!

00:15:56.930 --> 00:16:00.100
I threw you a laser beam,
straight as an arrow!

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:05.860
But you didn't think I'd throw anything
half as good, so you switched off!

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:08.980
As if. I'd never switch off on a play!

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.670
Where do ya get off, accusin' me like that?

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:12.110
'Cause it's true!

00:16:12.670 --> 00:16:14.830
You were in front of the
plate when you caught it,

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:17.700
meaning you were too slow
retiring the runner.

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:20.720
You totally underestimated 
my throw back to home!

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:25.060
And what's more, half of
Sakura-senpai's walks were your fault!

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:25.830
What?

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.300
You got her to paint the
corners from the first ball,

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:31.160
before she had time to find her groove.

00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:35.000
Everyone could see the batters
were watching her pitches,

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:38.160
so you should've got her to
throw strikes and cornered 'em.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.810
How stupid are you?!

00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:41.780
What did ya say?!

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:44.290
Ya don't know the first thing 'bout signalin'!

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:45.640
Hey, Nishina!

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:48.010
Base coach. You're our base coach.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.980
I don't know the finer details, sure.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.700
But even from the outfield, I could tell.

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:57.700
You made life seriously
tough for your pitcher.

00:17:05.570 --> 00:17:07.370
<i>Bottom of the first.</i>

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:09.840
<i>Fuurin Academy to bat.</i>

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:13.400
<i>Batting first, center field, Fujii-san.</i>

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:15.260
All right, time to strike back!

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.220
Let's change gear and get some hits!

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:19.510
Knock them out!

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:26.360
Say what? You got into Fuurin?!

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:27.220
Yeah.

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:32.180
For real? Their baseball team's
supposed to be pretty strong right now.

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:35.840
I heard they got themselves a coach
who knows his stuff a few years back.

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:38.070
Yeah, after hearing my
sister talk about him,

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:40.990
I decided I wanted him to train me too.

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:44.130
The baseball team even has their own field,

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:46.740
so I took my studies seriously for once.

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:49.670
Damn, man, I'm jealous.

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:53.460
Must be nice to have the smarts and
the money to go to a private school.

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:56.050
And what's more, Sakura's going there too.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:57.510
What?!

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:00.050
Are you freakin' kidding me?!

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:02.670
How can the world be <i>this</i> unfair?!

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:04.770
Wh-What did <i>I</i> do?

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:09.190
I guess we'll eventually face 
off in the district playoffs.

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:14.550
Let's all do our best.

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:17.000
We won't hold back when we face you.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:17.980
Yeah.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:21.410
Play!

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:30.380
Strike!

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:32.840
Wow. That's seriously fast.

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:41.260
Strike!

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.460
Huh? What was <i>that</i>?

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:45.960
It's like it just dropped out of the air!

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:47.480
A 12-6 curve, huh?

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:51.650
Strike!

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:52.650
Batter out!

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:55.740
I didn't realize a curveball
could break down like that.

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:58.520
And they can be fast <i>or</i> slow. This is bad.

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:08.760
Strike! You're out!

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:13.460
You can't get the timing right on those.

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.430
And he has amazing control.

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:19.130
<i>Wow, this guy's incredible.</i>

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:22.730
<i>I wish I could throw a curveball like that.</i>

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:27.600
<i>Batting third, second base, Sawa-san.</i>

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:30.270
<i>They were really strong up until last year.</i>

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:34.940
<i>But once they lost their coach, 
the girls became their top batters.</i>

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:37.590
<i>Shigeno's not what I expected, either.</i>

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:43.080
Strike!

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:45.760
<i>No matter how good these girls are,</i>

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.750
<i>hitting Urabe's pitches won't be easy.</i>

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:50.640
Timeout! Timeout!

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:54.620
Fuurin's next batter needs
to get into the on-deck circle!

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:56.320
Anita!

00:19:57.140 --> 00:19:58.370
Anita!

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.840
Oh. I'm up.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:10.690
Play!

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:17.910
<i>You were in front of the
plate when you caught it,</i>

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:20.800
<i>meaning you were too slow
retiring the runner.</i>

00:20:21.350 --> 00:20:25.620
<i>And what's more, half of
Sakura-senpai's walks were your fault!</i>

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:28.130
<i>He was right 'bout all of it.</i>

00:20:28.680 --> 00:20:33.040
<i>I also missed our chance to
regroup by callin' a timeout.</i>

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:36.250
<i>They scored a second run 'cause
I didn't see the runner on third</i>

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:39.620
<i>when I fell for the decoy
run of the runner on first.</i>

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:42.720
You're also being tested right now.

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:47.010
I'll spell it out for you.
I think Mutsuko can do it.

00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:53.000
If they end up hitting her pitches, 
that's on you as the catcher.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:59.110
<i>I didn't do everythin' in my power,
an' now they've scored two runs against us.</i>

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:06.860
What?!

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:09.460
Yes! Into center field!

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:11.290
Nice one, Yayoi!

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:12.990
<i>I flunked the test.</i>

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:18.930
<i>It's jus' like before. This proves it.
I'm a total failure as a catcher.</i>

00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:35.900
You're not concentrating.

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:38.250
Is your mind on something
other than batting?

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:40.030
Oh, uh, no...

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:41.320
I'm relieved.

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:42.070
Huh?

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:47.420
You're not a catcher if your mind's not
always on defense and game-calling.

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:51.030
You're more delicate than
I thought. That's a good thing.

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:57.210
You can't use the bat to erase 
the errors we made on defense,

00:21:57.210 --> 00:22:00.460
but you <i>can</i> use it to cancel
out the runs they took from us.

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:04.020
If you get the chance to help
the pitcher out with your bat,

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:07.710
it'd be a shame to let it pass you by
because you're beating yourself up.

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:23.230
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Kabashima-san.</i>

00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:02.680
I'm sorry, Sakura-senpai.

00:24:02.680 --> 00:24:05.000
S'all my fault they got two runs on the board.

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.630
Don't get so down on yourself.

00:24:06.970 --> 00:24:09.050
We can make up for those errors.

00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:11.420
You have your own strengths, Anita.

00:24:11.790 --> 00:24:13.840
I'll pay 'em back for those runs, just ya watch!

00:24:14.100 --> 00:24:17.720
I ain't throwin' in the towel
like I did back in Little League!

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:19.970
Back in Little League? Did something happen?

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>No Freakin' Way!</b>

00:24:20.210 --> 00:24:22.230
Next time: "No Freakin' Way!"

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:24.350
Run to the stage of yer dreams!
